<% render partial: 'about/subnav' %>

<div class="box wide">
  <div class="story_text">
  <p>
  <%= Rails.application.name %> is a forum where Liam Fox and his friends can discuss ideas, particularly those pertaining to philosophy, physics, and mathematics. I created this forum so that the many conversations I have can all exist in one place, and so that they have more permanence. I also believe that the Reddit-like nested trees of comments supported by this forum software are more conducive to complex conversations than programs ike WhatsApp are. Contact me, <a href="/moderators">the moderator</a>, with any questions or problems.
  </p>

  <h2 id="guidelines">Guidelines</h2>
  <div style="grid-column: 1 / -1;">
    <p>Please obey the following rules:</p>
    <ul style="list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.5em;">
      <li>If content is LLM generated (and if it's not obvious), you must disclose that it is.</li>
      <li>Keep profanity and insults to a minimum.</li>
      <li>No links to pirated content.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2 id="invitations">Invitations</h2>
  <p>
  <%= Rails.application.name %> is invite-only. The full <%= link_to 'user tree', users_tree_path %>
  is public, and each user's profile shows who invited them.
  Users are considered "new" for their first <%= User::NEW_USER_DAYS %> days,
  and their usernames appear <span class="new_user">in green</span>.
  New users can't send invites, flag, or use these tags:
  <% Tag.not_permitted_for_new_users.pluck(:tag).each do |t| %><%= link_to t, tag_path(t) %> <% end %>
  </p>
  <p>
  To get an invitation, ask someone you know who's already a member.
  </p>
  </div>
</div>
